      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict confirmed_shifted: insert_after_residue 349 -> 333 on human canonical P56975 (paper numbering: ortholog:mouse, construct species: mouse). Paper (PMID 35579602): \"carboxyl-terminal to L 362 [no deletion], P 358 [deltaTDHL], S 353 [deltaILSDP], or P 349 [deltaKTDS]) ... superscript numbers relative to full-length mouse proNRG3; GenBank accession number: NP_032760.1\". Audit note: Mouse proNRG3 construct; the paper's numbers match neither NP_032760.1 nor UniProt O35181 (both 713 aa; residue 349 is Gly, 353 Met, 358 Val). The deletion motifs KTDS/ILSDP/TDHL pin the sites at mouse P335/S339/P344 = human P333/S337/P342 within the identical PKTDSILSDPTDHLGIEF stretch, i.e. paper numbering is +16 vs human canonical. Results text swaps the deletions (deltaILSDP at P349) but the legend and sequence agree. Insertion at this site also deleted KTDS (human 334-337). Human 349 is Glu, not Pro. No surface labeling of LOV2 constructs; variant did not show the light-regulated phenotype.] L5 names mouse P349 as a LOV2 insertion site in full-length membrane-anchored mouse NRG3; the insertion was accompanied by a 5-residue deletion (\u0394ILSDP) C-terminal to the site, indicating local sequence modification was needed. Human NRG3 position 349 is E (seq[348]='E'), differing from mouse P349; the position is 12 residues from TM2 (361), safely within the >=3-residue margin. This is indirect/inferred evidence from a mouse ortholog, and the required deletion lowers confidence. Full-length mouse proNRG3 (NP_032760.1) with the LOV2/J\u03b1 domain inserted at mouse P349, accompanied by deletion of 5 residues (\u0394ILSDP) carboxyl-terminal to the insertion site. Constructs expressed in hippocampal neurons for photoactivation experiments.",
