      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict confirmed_shifted: insert_after_residue 358 -> 342 on human canonical P56975 (paper numbering: ortholog:mouse, construct species: mouse). Paper (PMID 35579602): \"carboxyl-terminal to L 362 [no deletion], P 358 [deltaTDHL], S 353 [deltaILSDP], or P 349 [deltaKTDS]) ... superscript numbers relative to full-length mouse proNRG3; GenBank accession number: NP_032760.1\". Audit note: Mouse proNRG3 construct; the paper's numbers match neither NP_032760.1 nor UniProt O35181 (both 713 aa; residue 349 is Gly, 353 Met, 358 Val). The deletion motifs KTDS/ILSDP/TDHL pin the sites at mouse P335/S339/P344 = human P333/S337/P342 within the identical PKTDSILSDPTDHLGIEF stretch, i.e. paper numbering is +16 vs human canonical. Results text swaps the deletions (deltaILSDP at P349) but the legend and sequence agree. Insertion at this site also deleted TDHL (human 343-346). Human 358 is Gln, not Pro. Variant did not show the light-regulated phenotype; no surface labeling.] L5 names mouse P358 as a LOV2 insertion site in full-length membrane-anchored mouse NRG3; the insertion required a 4-residue deletion (\u0394TDHL) C-terminal to the site. Human NRG3 position 358 is Q (seq[357]='Q'), differing from mouse P358; the position is exactly 3 residues from TM2 (361), at the minimum allowed distance. This is indirect/inferred evidence from a mouse ortholog, the required deletion lowers confidence, and the proximity to TM2 is borderline. Full-length mouse proNRG3 (NP_032760.1) with the LOV2/J\u03b1 domain inserted at mouse P358, accompanied by deletion of 4 residues (\u0394TDHL) carboxyl-terminal to the insertion site. Constructs expressed in hippocampal neurons for photoactivation experiments.",
